node_modules/
# The name in every form, not only as a directory: a worktree with node_modules
# as a SYMLINK once got that symlink committed by `git add -A`, and checking the
# commit out replaced the real tree with a link to itself.
/node_modules
node_modules
.next/
.next-old/
# The two transient names the atomic build reclaim uses (TASK-729): the
# shared claim a rename hands to exactly one reclaimer, and the private
# tree it moves the outgoing .next aside into. Both must be ignored for the
# same reason .next-old is — an update runs `git clean -fd` over this tree,
# and a claim swept away mid-flight is a box with no build.
.next-claim.*/
.next-discard.*/
out/
build/
coverage/
data/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.DS_Store
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.template
!.env.test.example
.update-branch
# install.sh writes the pin through an mktemp file alongside it and renames it
# into place, so the write cannot follow a symlink. It exists for microseconds
# and is removed if any step fails, but a run killed mid-write must not leave
# the device's working tree dirty forever.
.update-branch.*
# Orphan deploy marker from the pre-3.9 deploy method: nothing in this repo
# writes or reads it, but boxes that were deployed by hand still carry one. Left
# untracked it counted as a dirty working tree, so the About screen accused a
# healthy box of "not running the code on its disk" and every build stamped
# itself `dirty: true` (hwtest-round1, 2026-08-24). Ignored here so the artifact
# cannot fake drift; the updater deletes any it finds.
.deployed-sha
claude-code-source-code/
code-source-code/
.omx/
playwright-report/
test-results/
e2e-install/cache/
scripts/nm-dispatcher-failover.sh
.claude/

# Local debug scripts (per-session sandbox)
.scratch/

# Python bytecode (scripts/ has .py helpers; the cache is never shipped)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
bench/results/
